.page df 1 report free space on mounted filesystems

# SYNOPSIS
*df* [*-hkTaP*] [_PATH_ ...]

# DESCRIPTION
`df` shows how much room each mounted filesystem has left: its size, what is used, what is available, the percentage used and where it is mounted. With no _PATH_ it lists every filesystem in `/proc/mounts` that holds anything (the in-memory root and `/BambooForest`, a mounted HUMANVILLAGE disk, ...); with paths it reports the filesystem each path lives on. A filesystem mounted read-only is marked `(ro)`. On a terminal a short banner from Keine, who keeps the ledger, is printed first.

# OPTIONS
@ *-h*
    Sizes in a human-readable form (`1.4M`) instead of 1 KiB blocks.
@ *-k*
    1 KiB blocks (the default).
@ *-T*
    Add a column with the filesystem type (`tmpfs`, `fat32`, ...).
@ *-a*
    Also list filesystems with no blocks (`/proc`, `/dev`).
@ *-P*
    POSIX output: no banner.

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if a path could not be examined.

# EXAMPLES
    df -h
    df -T /HumanVillage

# SEE ALSO
mount(8), umount(8), du(1)
